hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"72","\The Negus [the Emperor of Ethiopia] gave the Prophet (Allah bless him and give him peace) a pair of plain black socks"","" so he put them on"","" then performed the minor ritual ablution and wiped over them.”"""""
"73","\Dihya [a notable Companion of his] gave the Prophet (Allah bless him and give him peace) a pair of plain black socks"","" so he wore them"",""\""— and Isra’il said"","" on the authority of Jabir"","" on the authority of 'Amir: \""[He also gave him] a gown"","" so he wore the socks until they were perforated"","" without the Prophet (Allah bless him and give him peace) knowing whether they were tanned or not.”"""""
